                <pb facs="0596" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 814.48/65</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leavell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-13T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Joint Committee of American and Guatemalan Red Cross are endeavoring to arrange
                    program of operations to clean city of filth which the President promises put
                    through. Unless this is done thoroughly and promptly, disastrous epidemics are
                    inevitable, for all open spaces are jammed and the people are without necessary
                    conveniences.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leavell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
